    "body": "Have 2 simple controllers for matching routes.\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nvar PagesController = can.Control({\r\n  ':id route' : function(data) {\r\n    this.element.text(\"PagesController match\")\r\n  }\r\n});\r\n\r\nvar WorkshopController = can.Control({\r\n  'workshop route' : function(data) {\r\n    this.element.text(\"WorkshopController match\")\r\n  }\r\n});\r\n```\r\nnow bind them\r\n```javascript\r\nnew PagesController('body', {})\r\nnew WorkshopController('body', {})\r\n```\r\nand set route\r\n```javascript\r\nwindow.location.hash = \"workshop\"\r\n```\r\nresult of text in body is `PagesController match`\r\n\r\nI completely understand why is this happening. Router match first route which can be applied. It is like in almost every backend routers. But in these you can control order of them. Otherwise in dynamic page with javascript mostly you can't. Personally have no specific idea how to do this (maybe router can inside reorder routes based on absolute path and path with wildcard?).\r\n\r\nplayground http://jsbin.com/oCUSaYa/4/edit?html,js,console,output\r\n"
