    "body": "This is a follow up on issue #157 (#234, #241, #321, #342, #343) and also related to #488. Some HTML attributes need special treatment when live binding:\r\n\r\n- __src__ - Should not be set with the live binding placeholder (`__!!__`) because it triggers a request to `__!!__`.\r\n- __style__ - Can not be set in IE with the live binding placeholder (e.g. `style=\"background-color: {{color}}\"` -> `background-color: __!!__`) because IE tries to parse it into a CSS stylesheet and just drops any illegal CSS. It also looks like the attribute shouldn't be set using `element.setAttribute('style')` but `element.style.cssText` instead."
