    "body": "I'd like to make the following API changes for 1.3 while retaining backwards compatibility:\r\n\r\n## Make .extend the documented way to create a new Constructor function\r\n\r\n```js\r\ncan.Construct.extend(STATIC, PROTOTYPE)\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor 1.4, .extend will be necessary.  Allowing people to create a list w/o new like: `can.List()`.\r\n\r\n## Rename Observe and Map\r\n\r\n```js\r\ncan.Observe -> can.Map\r\ncan.Observe.List -> can.List\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Rename can.view to can.template\r\n\r\n```js\r\ncan.template(\"foo.mustache\",{})\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Split can.compute into can.observe (or can.observable) and can.compute\r\n\r\n_this one needs some extra thought_\r\n\r\nSingle value:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nfive = can.observe(5)\r\n```\r\n\r\nSetter:\r\n```js\r\nvar age = can.compute(0,function(newVal, oldVal){\r\n    var num = +newVal\r\n    if(! isNaN(num) && 0 <= num && num <= 120 ){\r\n        return num;\r\n    } else {\r\n        return oldVal;\r\n    }\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n"
